The Stony Brook Scale (SBS) is a behaviour rating scale which&#13;
is clamed to have the ability to sub-categorize highly selected&#13;
groups of hyperactive children &lt;0’U*ry * Steen,&#13;
1982). in particular, it has been suggested that this scale&#13;
can differentiate between purely hyperactive and aggressive&#13;
children. B * present study sought to replicate the research&#13;
of 0' Leary and Steen (1982) and to extend the application of&#13;
the Stony Brook Scale to parent ratings of child behaviour.&#13;
